       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe order may have been meant as one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg per dose.** These are other common strengths.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you meant, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest adding a note with the rationale as well."
